Add --codec to ModelQuantizer, and stop narrowing BF16 rows to F16

Every arm opens with Tensor<FloatType>(from: tensor), which silently narrows
BF16 matmul weights to F16. Z-Image and the Qwen family carry CCV_16BF rows
inside their _f16 checkpoints, the codecs keep centroids and row scales in the
tensor's own dtype, and ccv_nnc_tensor_read has no 16F to 16BF path, so the
result crashes the server on first generation. The fix preserves any
already-16-bit row and still narrows anything else.

--codec replaces the per-version recipe's codec for the matmul bulk only,
which is the same split the app's three quantize actions make. default
reproduces current output byte for byte. Palettizing is DP-bound and takes
hours on a 22B DiT where i8x is about eight passes per row, and the i8x
artifact is separately the only encoding an Apple Neural Engine can consume.
